{"report": "The volatility regime shows genuine stability, with no material shift in underlying pressures. The most recent VIX level of 9.51 sits squarely at the lower end of the observed range, having just retraced a brief spike to 12.12 two observations ago. That spike appears to have been transitory—not sustained. The vol_risk_premium has compressed to 0.02, the lowest in the dataset, suggesting dampened near-term tail hedging demand relative to implied vol itself. The 4-week momentum (vix_change_4w) of -0.62 points reinforces ease, with VIX pulling back from elevated levels that peaked at 15.51 several observations prior.

